# Section edge alignment (Winter Website)

For full-width content bands (stats, grids, rows of items):

1. Use **10% left and right padding** on the section (`padding-inline: 10%`).
2. Do **not** use equal `1fr` columns with left-aligned text — the last item will look more inset than the first.
3. Instead, size items to their content and pin the first/last to the padded edges:

```css
section {
  padding-inline: 10%;
}
.row {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(N, max-content);
  justify-content: space-between;
  width: 100%;
}
```

Result: first block aligns to the left 10% edge, last block to the right 10% edge, same inset on both sides.

Reference implementation: `facts-section` / `facts-grid` in `src/app/globals.css`.
